    "result_text": "The build passes. The test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email rejection in the owner-creation flow at `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, following the existing validation conventions:\n\n1. **Added a blocklist constant** \u2014 `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` = `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}`, alongside the existing `EMAIL_PATTERN`.\n\n2. **Extended `normalizeEmail`** \u2014 after the syntactic check and lower-casing, it extracts the domain (everything after `@`) and, if it's on the blocklist, throws `InvalidFieldValueException(\"email\", ...)`. Since the value is already canonicalized to lowercase before the check, domains like `X@MAILINATOR.COM` are also caught.\n\n3. **Added the `java.util.Set` import.**\n\nThe `InvalidFieldValueException` is already mapped by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` to **400 Bad Request**, so no new exception handler was needed. The check reuses the existing email-validation entry point, so it only runs when an email is supplied (email remains optional). The new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes and the full build is green.",
